    "result_text": "The full suite consists of just `AcceptanceTest` (the others are an abstract base and a helper), and it passes. The build is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `membershipNumber` assignment formatted `<customerCode>-M<YY>`, where `YY` is the last two digits of the `registrationDate` year.\n\nSince `membershipNumber` is fully derived from the owner's own stored fields (`customerCode` and `registrationDate`), I followed the existing pattern used for other derived read-only fields (`displayName`, `initials`) rather than persisting a new column:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `membershipNumber` property to the `Owner` schema (so the generated `OwnerDto` gets the field).\n\n2. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `membershipNumber(owner)` helper and mapped it in `toOwnerDto`:\n   ```java\n   int yy = owner.getRegistrationDate().getYear() % 100;\n   return String.format(\"%s-M%02d\", owner.getCustomerCode(), yy);\n   ```\n   It returns `null` when either source field is absent, so it degrades gracefully.\n\nThe `%02d` zero-pads the year (e.g. year 2007 \u2192 `M07`), matching the spec example `SMI-0007-M26`. `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS**.",
